<article class="env-lemma" id="0DTH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DTH">Lemma <span data-tag="0DTH">100.11.13</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. Let $x \in |\mathcal{X}|$ with image $y \in |\mathcal{Y}|$. If the residual gerbes $\mathcal{Z}_ x \subset \mathcal{X}$ and $\mathcal{Z}_ y \subset \mathcal{Y}$ of $x$ and $y$ exist, then $f$ induces a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{X} \ar[d]_ f &  \mathcal{Z}_ x \ar[l] \ar[d] \\  \mathcal{Y} &  \mathcal{Z}_ y \ar[l] }  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a field $k$ and a surjective, flat, locally finitely presented morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to \mathcal{Z}_ x$. The morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to \mathcal{Y}$ factors through $\mathcal{Z}_ y$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/06MW" data-tag="06MW">100.11.11</a>. Thus $\mathcal{Z}_ x \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{Z}_ y$ is a nonempty substack of $\mathcal{Z}_ x$ hence equal to $\mathcal{Z}_ x$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/06MQ" data-tag="06MQ">100.11.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>